        {
            "id": "control-flow",
            "title": "Control Flow",
            "pages": [
                {
                    "content": "Control flow decides which code runs. The if statement runs code only when a condition is true. Use else for code that runs when the condition is false.",
                    "code": [
                        "if",
                        "else"
                    ],
                    "examples": [
                        "if score > 10:",
                        "    print(\"High score!\")",
                        "else:",
                        "    print(\"Keep trying\")"
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "content": "elif means else if. It checks another condition when the previous condition was false. You can place several elif branches between if and else.",
                    "code": [
                        "elif"
                    ],
                    "examples": [
                        "if score >= 90:",
                        "    print(\"A\")",
                        "elif score >= 80:",
                        "    print(\"B\")",
                        "else:",
                        "    print(\"Try again\")"
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "content": "Python uses indentation, not curly braces, to define blocks of code. Statements inside conditions and loops must be indented, usually by four spaces. Incorrect indentation causes an error.",
                    "code": [],
                    "examples": [
                        "if True:",
                        "    print(\"Inside\")",
                        "print(\"Outside\")"
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "content": "Loops repeat code. A while loop repeats while a condition remains true. A for loop repeats code for each item in a sequence.",
                    "code": [
                        "while",
                        "for"
                    ],
                    "examples": [
                        "count = 0",
                        "while count < 3:",
                        "    count += 1",
                        "for item in items:",
                        "    print(item)"
                    ]
                }
            ],
            "quiz": [
                {
                    "question": "Which statement is used to execute code only when a condition is true?",
                    "choices": [
                        "for",
                        "def",
                        "return",
                        "if"
