        {
            "id": "functions",
            "title": "Functions",
            "pages": [
                {
                    "content": "A function is a reusable block of code. Define one with the def keyword, a name, parentheses, and a colon. The indented lines below are the function's body.",
                    "code": [
                        "def"
                    ],
                    "examples": [
                        "def greet():",
                        "    print(\"Hello!\")",
                        "greet()"
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "content": "Parameters are inputs defined by the function; they receive values when the function is called. The return keyword sends a value back to the code that called the function.",
                    "code": [
                        "return"
                    ],
                    "examples": [
                        "def add(a, b):",
                        "    return a + b"
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "content": "Calling add(2, 3) returns 5. Python functions start with def and end the first line with a colon. Words like function, func, and define, or curly braces, are not Python.",
                    "code": [
                        "add(2, 3)",
                        "def"
                    ],
                    "examples": [
                        "def add(a, b):",
                        "    return a + b",
                        "total = add(2, 3)",
                        "print(total)  # 5"
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "content": "In short: variables store values, control flow controls execution, and functions provide reusable blocks of code. Together they let programs make decisions and avoid repeating work.",
                    "code": [],
                    "examples": [
                        "def grade(score):",
                        "    if score >= 90:",
                        "        return \"A\"",
                        "    return \"B\""
                    ]
                }
            ],
